#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=8 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974094182'; [Fri Nov 06 15:08:14 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!A metric on 24 points: the example of Imrich, Simoes-Pereira and Zamfirescu (1984), On optimal embeddings of
metrics in graphs, J. Combin. Theory B 36:1-15, transcribed from the paper. RazorNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 24 taxa and a 24 x 24 distance matrix.
The Razor Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 30 nodes and 36 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 28 nodes and 30 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

